<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Entitlements for serberusd. NOT used by any build: the Xcode serberusd
  target signs without entitlements (a command-line tool cannot embed the
  provisioning profile the restricted ES entitlement needs, so AMFI would kill
  it), and the shipped bundle is signed with
  Support/serberusd-distribution.entitlements. Kept as a record of the one
  code entitlement the daemon uses.

  The daemon needs no special code entitlements in V1:
    * Hardened Runtime is a signing flag, not an entitlement.
    * The Mach service is granted via the LaunchDaemon plist's MachServices
      key, not an entitlement.
    * System Keychain access for the HMAC keys works for a root
      daemon without a keychain-access-group entitlement.
    * Full Disk Access is granted via a PPPC configuration profile, not a
      code entitlement.

  The Endpoint Security client entitlement is granted by Apple on request, per
  team. Embedding a *restricted* entitlement requires a provisioning
  profile that authorizes it; a profile-less local Apple-Development signature
  cannot carry it (AMFI rejects at launch). The daemon tolerates ESF being
  unavailable (logs and runs without exec enforcement), so unit/integration
  tests and the prompt round-trip do not require it.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>com.apple.developer.endpoint-security.client</key>
    <true/>
</dict>
</plist>
